:: HideAndSeek [childhood]
# Sharpening the Senses

You join several children in a game of hide and seek around the camp. One child covers their eyes and counts slowly while the rest of you scatter to find hiding places.

You look around quickly, considering your options. Behind a shelter? Too obvious. Near the storage area? The adults might not approve. Finally, you spot a perfect place - a small depression near some baskets, partially covered by a hide that's been set out to dry.

You curl up small, trying to control your breathing and remain still. These are the same skills hunters use to avoid detection by animals or rival tribes.

As you wait, you listen carefully to the sounds around you - footsteps approaching and receding, the seeker finding other children, the normal sounds of camp life continuing around your game.

<<if gameUtils.hasSkillLevelIncreased("perception")>>
  <div class="skill-message">
    <span class="skill-increase">Your perception has improved!</span>
  </div>
<</if>>

<<link "Try to move to a better hiding spot without being seen">>
  <<set $skills.perception += 0.2>>
  <<goto "ImproveHiding">>
<</link>>

<<link "Stay perfectly still until the game ends">>
  <<goto "StayHidden">>
<</link>>